==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|peritonaeum}}

===Etymology===
From {{derived|en|la|peritonaeum}}, from {{derived|la|grc|περιτόναιον}}, from {{mention|grc|περιτόναιος|t=stretched or strained over}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌpɛɹ.ɪt.əˈniː.əm/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|peritonea}}
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} In [[mammal]]s, the [[serous membrane]] lining the cavity of the abdomen and that is folded over the [[viscera]].
# {{lb|en|zoology}} In [[animal]]s, the membrane lining the [[coelom]] cavity.

====Derived terms====
{{der3|en|hydroperitoneum|pleuroperitoneum|retroperitoneum|pneumoperitoneum|peritoneal|peritoneally|peritonitis}}

